                    <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-1">8. Create pagination helper methods</div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-2">
                        Use a computed property to slice the filtered list for the current page. Previous/Next methods
                        update
                        the page number with bounds checking to prevent going out of range.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="list-disc ml-4 mb-2 text-[11px] text-gray-600 space-y-1">
                        <li><code>CurrentPagePokemon</code> is a computed property using <code>=&gt;</code> syntax</li>
                        <li><code>Skip((currentPage - 1) * pageSize)</code> skips to the right position in the list</li>
                        <li><code>Take(pageSize)</code> grabs exactly 20 Pokemon for this page</li>
                        <li><code>if (currentPage &gt; 1)</code> prevents going below page 1</li>
                        <li><code>if (currentPage &lt; totalPages)</code> prevents going past the last page</li>
                    </ul>
                    <pre class="code-block text-xs font-mono text-gray-800">private int currentPage = 1;
private int pageSize = 20;
private int totalPages =&gt; (int)Math.Ceiling(filteredPokemon.Count / (double)pageSize);

private List&lt;PokemonListItem&gt; CurrentPagePokemon =&gt; filteredPokemon
    .Skip((currentPage - 1) * pageSize)
    .Take(pageSize)
    .ToList();

private void PreviousPage()
{
    if (currentPage &gt; 1) currentPage--;
}

private void NextPage()
{
    if (currentPage &lt; totalPages) currentPage++;
}</pre>
